---
import MakerLayout from '../layouts/MakerLayout.astro';
---
<MakerLayout title="PARADOX — Delegate the work to AI" description="PARADOX is an AI agent workspace for research, coding, studying, writing and product work. Give it an outcome and let it execute multi-step work.">
<main class="front">
  <section class="front-hero">
    <div class="front-nav"><span>PARADOX / 2026</span><span>AGENT OS</span><a href="/studio/">OPEN STUDIO ↗</a></div>
    <div class="front-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow"><i></i> NOT ANOTHER TOOL DIRECTORY</p><h1>Give it a job.<br/><em>Get the work.</em></h1><p class="lede">PARADOX turns a vague outcome into research, reasoning and a finished deliverable. One agent. Live public sources. Zero calculator clutter.</p><a class="launch" href="#agent">START WITH AN OUTCOME ↘</a></div>
      <div class="signal"><div class="signal-core">PX</div><div class="sig s1">RESEARCH</div><div class="sig s2">CODE</div><div class="sig s3">STUDY</div><div class="sig s4">WRITE</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="agent-zone" id="agent">
    <aside class="agent-sidebar"><span>01</span><strong>DELEGATE</strong><p>Describe what “done” looks like.</p><button class="preset" data-prompt="Research the best open-source LLMs for coding in 2026. Compare current evidence from GitHub, Hugging Face and developer discussions, then recommend one for a student project.">RESEARCH THE WEB</button><button class="preset" data-prompt="Turn this product idea into an investor-ready product brief with problem, users, differentiation, UX, architecture, MVP and launch strategy: a social app for discovering local events through AI.">BUILD A PRODUCT</button><button class="preset" data-prompt="Act as my software engineering interview coach. Start a realistic interview, ask one question at a time, adapt to my answers and finish with a scorecard and precise improvement plan.">COACH ME</button></aside>
    <section class="agent-main">
      <div class="agent-head"><span>LIVE AGENT</span><span id="modelBadge">MODEL NOT CONNECTED</span><button id="connectBtn">CONNECT MODEL</button></div>
      <textarea id="mission" placeholder="Example: Find the best current open-source coding model for me. Use live GitHub, Hugging Face and Hacker News evidence, compare the options, and give me a final recommendation with sources."></textarea>
      <div class="agent-controls"><select id="provider"><option value="openrouter">OPENROUTER / FREE ROUTER</option><option value="gemini">GEMINI DEVELOPER API</option><option value="huggingface">HUGGING FACE ROUTER</option></select><select id="style"><option>Actionable report</option><option>Deep research</option><option>Product spec</option><option>Study pack</option><option>Interview coach</option></select><button id="runAgent">RUN AGENT ↗</button></div>
      <article id="result" class="output"><div class="empty"><b>PX</b><p>The agent is waiting.</p><small>Connect a model, describe an outcome, and run it.</small></div></article>
    </section>
  </section>

  <section class="proof"><article><span>02 / LIVE TOOLS</span><h2>It can leave the page.</h2><p>The agent can query public Wikipedia, GitHub, Hugging Face and Hacker News data, then synthesize the evidence.</p></article><article><span>03 / NO FAKE AI</span><h2>Real model calls.</h2><p>PARADOX supports OpenRouter’s free-model router, Gemini and Hugging Face. The model actually generates the response.</p></article><article><span>04 / PRODUCT LOOP</span><h2>Research → answer → return.</h2><p>Sessions remain useful because the product is built around outcomes, not a hundred disconnected buttons.</p></article></section>
</main>
<script type="module" src="../scripts/studio.js"></script>
<style>
.front{background:#090b0b;color:#eee;min-height:100vh}.front-hero{min-height:100svh;padding:18px clamp(18px,4vw,65px) 50px;background:radial-gradient(circle at 78% 23%,rgba(217,255,63,.13),transparent 24%),#090b0b}.front-nav{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;border-bottom:1px solid #303331;padding-bottom:14px;font:9px 'DM Mono';letter-spacing:.14em;color:#8d908a}.front-nav a{color:#d9ff3f}.front-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr .8fr;align-items:center;min-height:82svh;gap:6vw}.eyebrow{font:9px 'DM Mono';letter-spacing:.16em;color:#999}.eyebrow i{display:inline-block;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:#ff5638;margin-right:8px}.front h1{font:700 clamp(78px,11vw,165px)/.76 'DM Sans';letter-spacing:-.09em;margin:30px 0}.front h1 em{font-family:'Instrument Serif';font-weight:400;letter-spacing:-.06em;color:#d9ff3f}.lede{max-width:650px;color:#9b9e96;font-size:18px;line-height:1.55}.launch,.agent-controls button,#connectBtn{display:inline-block;background:#d9ff3f;color:#090b0b;border:0;padding:14px 17px;font:9px 'DM Mono';margin-top:28px}.signal{height:520px;position:relative;display:grid;place-items:center}.signal:before,.signal:after{content:'';position:absolute;border:1px solid #303331;border-radius:50%;width:90%;height:55%;transform:rotate(22deg)}.signal:after{width:66%;height:78%;transform:rotate(-55deg)}.signal-core{width:170px;height:170px;border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;background:#d9ff3f;color:#090b0b;font:700 53px 'DM Sans';box-shadow:18px 18px 0 #ff5638;position:relative;z-index:2}.sig{position:absolute;border:1px solid #3b3d39;padding:8px 10px;font:8px 'DM Mono';background:#0e1110}.s1{top:13%;left:8%}.s2{top:23%;right:6%}.s3{bottom:18%;left:4%}.s4{bottom:8%;right:13%}
.agent-zone{background:#f2efe7;color:#0d0e0e;display:grid;grid-template-columns:260px 1fr;min-height:840px}.agent-sidebar{border-right:1px solid #bbb8b0;padding:30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px}.agent-sidebar>span{font:9px 'DM Mono';color:#ff5638}.agent-sidebar strong{font:11px 'DM Mono';letter-spacing:.13em}.agent-sidebar p{color:#6d6e68;font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;margin-bottom:22px}.preset{background:transparent;border:1px solid #b7b5ac;text-align:left;padding:13px;font:9px 'DM Mono'}.preset:hover{background:#fff;transform:translateX(4px)}.agent-main{padding:30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px}.agent-head,.agent-controls{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px}.agent-head{justify-content:space-between;border-bottom:1px solid #bbb8b0;padding-bottom:12px;font:9px 'DM Mono'}.agent-head span:nth-child(2){color:#777970;margin-left:auto}.agent-head button{margin:0;background:transparent;border:1px solid #aaa79e;padding:9px;font:8px 'DM Mono'}.agent-main textarea{width:100%;min-height:260px;resize:vertical;background:#fff;border:1px solid #bbb8b0;padding:20px;font:17px/1.55 'DM Sans';outline:0}.agent-controls select{flex:1;background:#e8e4db;border:0;padding:12px;font:9px 'DM Mono';outline:0}.agent-controls button{margin:0;white-space:nowrap;background:#0d0e0e;color:white}.output{flex:1;min-height:420px;background:#0d0f0f;color:#e9e8e0;padding:25px;overflow:auto}.empty{min-height:360px;display:grid;place-items:center;text-align:center}.empty b{font:700 78px 'DM Sans';color:#d9ff3f}.empty p{margin:0;font-size:17px}.empty small{color:#757a73}.output h2{font:600 28px 'DM Sans'}.output pre{white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;font:12px/1.7 'DM Mono'}.output .source{font:9px 'DM Mono';color:#92978f;margin-top:20px}.output a{color:#d9ff3f}.result-error{padding:25px;border:1px solid #56261d;color:#ff9e89}.proof{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);background:#f2efe7;color:#0d0e0e;border-top:1px solid #bbb8b0}.proof article{padding:40px;border-right:1px solid #bbb8b0}.proof article:last-child{border:0}.proof span{font:9px 'DM Mono';color:#ff5638}.proof h2{font:400 44px/.9 'Instrument Serif';margin:22px 0}.proof p{max-width:330px;color:#666861;line-height:1.6}
@media(max-width:900px){.front-grid,.agent-zone,.proof{grid-template-columns:1fr}.signal{height:390px}.agent-sidebar{border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid #bbb8b0}.proof article{border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid #bbb8b0}.agent-main{padding:18px}}@media(max-width:560px){.front h1{font-size:76px}.lede{font-size:16px}.front-nav span:nth-child(2){display:none}.agent-controls{flex-direction:column;align-items:stretch}.agent-controls select,.agent-controls button{width:100%}}
</style>
</MakerLayout>
